One more consideration for "whole world visible": with N=72 and heights up to ~20, the world spans ~72 units. I'll frame the camera at distance ~95 with fov 45, target at village centre, and auto-rotate azimuth slowly via `controls.autoRotate`-style manual orbit (I'll implement orbit myself to avoid importing OrbitControls from a separate file — the spec only gives three.module.js, so a hand-rolled orbit with pointer drag + wheel zoom + auto-rotation is the right call).

